Logorama is a 2009 French adult animated satirical short film produced by the French graphic
design and animation studio H5 as their first and only cinematic project.

11
00:10:21,176 --> 00:10:27,176
Co-written and directed by François Alaux, Hervé de Crécy and Ludovic Houplain, the film is set in a stylized version of Los Angeles and portrays
various events as being told entirely through the extensive use of more than 2,000 contemporary and historical company logos and mascots.

